# RUNTIME STATE — must NEVER be baked into the image.
# `COPY data/ ./data/` copies the whole working tree, including untracked files, so
# any of these left lying around locally ships to production. This is not
# theoretical: a stale data/last_analytics_pull.json (Sep 20) was baked into every
# build and made the app report a fixed ~41h-old "last pull", which in turn made
# every fresh container believe it was due. That accidental behaviour was the only
# thing masking a missed anchor, and it hid the real freshness state from QA.
# The durable source of truth is now D1 (app_state); these files are local-only.
data/last_analytics_pull.json
data/last_cache_warm.json
data/last_cache_warm_error.json
data/d1_rankings_last.json
data/fcs_extras_progress.json
